No conversion guides were used at any point, per your instruction. Notably, most agents were also given the actual Fortran source (`KernSmooth/src/*.f`) rather than reconstructions, since I found it in the repo partway through — this let most conversions be validated numerically against real R output (many matched to floating-point precision, e.g. `locpoly`, `sdiag`, `dpih`, `dpik`, `dpill` all cross-checked against a live R+KernSmooth install). I also caught and fixed one bug directly: the first `rlbin` conversion (done before I found the Fortran source) was missing a right-endpoint boundary correction that only `rlbin.f` has (not `linbin.f`), which I patched by hand.
